<title>USA: Fannie Mae Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			   $0.65		    $0.37</p>
<p> Net			 712,100		  408,300</p>
<p> Net int income	  923,100		  840,200</p>
<p> Loan loss prov	   50,000		   35,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		1,073,400		1,103,300</p>
<p>		 YEAR</p>
<p> Shr			   $2.48		    $1.95</p>
<p> Net		     2,724,700		2,144,200</p>
<p> Net int income	3,592,300		3,047,400</p>
<p> Loan loss prov	  195,000		  140,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		1,083,300		1,102,400</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Net for both years includes charge for early extinguishment of debt. Shr excluding charge is $2.50 vs $1.96.</p>
<p>Total assets, including assets off balance sheet, were $891.99 bln at 1996 year end.</p>
<p>Federal National Mortgage Association.</p>
</text>
